MIRA Green Retrofit Audit

Lab: Defend your stack's carbon story
Path: Path B - green retrofit audit of an existing bootcamp artifact
Artifact: MIRA AI-assisted photoshoot-planning MVP

Submission files

File

Purpose

MIRA_green_retrofit_carbon_story.pptx

Main deliverable: title slide plus 12 content slides. Includes the assessment defense, four-pillar map, four proposed solutions, measurement plan, caveats and before/after hypotheses. Speaker notes contain presenter guidance and source links.

mira_green_retrofit_audit.md

Completed Path B retrofit audit, three-row lever table, prioritised recommendations, measurement plan, trade-offs and Green Software Foundation pattern references.

mira_artifact_reference.md

Concise reference to the existing MIRA artifact, user journey, architecture and audit boundary.

README.md

Maps the committed files and explains the submission scope.

Deck compliance check

Path B is explicit on the title slide.

The deck contains 12 content slides plus a title slide.

The primary audience is named on slide 1.

One functional unit, R, is defined on slide 2.

Hotspots, assumptions, uncertainty and a skeptical stakeholder challenge are covered before the recommendations.

Four improvements are each mapped to at least one pillar and relevant named patterns.

The measurement plan uses the same functional unit and includes quality/latency guardrails.

The deck avoids claims that MIRA is carbon neutral or that cost automatically equals carbon.

Scope

This repository should contain only the four files listed above. No application code, personal files or unrelated bootcamp work is required for this lab submission.
